From 9d8e2a143f8c5a5514545460b5c3c24860c8bf60 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "sh.chao" <sh.chao@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 17 Jul 2026 12:27:25 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] r25-1-0087: batch exact path-state packets

Reduce the remaining dense-tile execution cost after 0086 without changing
candidate selection or pixel ownership. Consecutive visible stroke-only
commands are collected in fixed 256-command, 16384-point packets. A packet
shares only resolved stroke color, fill options, graph-state identity, AGG
renderer setup, and reusable raster scratch.

Every PDF path keeps its own live geometry, matrix, rasterization, and
destination composite in painter order. Text, fills, unsupported state,
transparent strokes, state changes, capacity limits, and cancellation remain
hard boundaries. The existing direct-path predicate is checked immediately
before buffering; the packet layer does not duplicate it or retain page-object
pointers beyond one synchronous render call.

Add bounded packet metrics and an exact fallback implementation for non-AGG
drivers. No Kotlin/JNI policy, cache, scheduler, lock, copied geometry, or
alternate rasterizer is introduced.

